  "_about": "Inside Maple Grove's shops (scripts/interiors.gd). Keys are the building models (assets/props/building_<id>.glb). Positions are in the building's own space in metres: x across (+x is on your right as you look at the front from the street), z from the back wall (-) to the front wall with the door (+). The door is at x 0 in the front wall. 'furniture': a furniture id (data/furniture.json), 'at' [x, z], 'turn' in degrees (0 = its front toward the door, 90 = toward +x, -90 = toward -x, 180 = toward the back wall). 'keeper': where the shopkeeper (villagers.json 'works_in') stands, where you stand to talk to them, how far they potter about (x, z), and which way they face. 'outside': [x, z, w, d] rects of the things standing in front of the building (baskets, signs, posts), which block the way. 'light': where the lamp hangs. Optional: 'room' [centre x, centre z, width, depth] when the room doesn't fill the lot (the Coffee Shop's terrace is in front of it), 'door_x', 'wall_block' (how deep the walls block the walking grid), and per piece 'y' (stood on something, no blocker) and 'read': 'seat' | 'shelf' with 'seat' [x, y, z, turn] and 'stand' [x, z] in the piece's own space (interiors.gd ReadSpot), or 'seats': [{'seat', 'stand'}, ...] for a piece with more than one (a café table's two chairs, the sofa). The Coffee Shop's 'visits' are the regulars who drop in for a coffee and a book (scripts/cafe_visits.gd): who, the hours [from, to], how often one comes in and how long they stay (game hours, [least, most]), how many at once, and where they stand at the counters to order [[x, z], ...]. 'wood': true lays the photo-scanned wood (scripts/building_skin.gd, wood_*) on the floor, tinted 'floor_colour', and on every piece's walnut, oak and *_wood surfaces.",
